$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=30))>0 as c0,position($q$and the first agreed dates are now kept as **Committed** dates$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=30))>0 as c1,position($q$| **Status** | Lifecycle: {neutral:Not Started}, {accent:In Progress}, {success:Completed}, {purple:Paused}, {danger:Cancelled}. Stays Not Started while the project is in Draft. |$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=14))>0 as c2,position($q$| **Phase** | Pipeline stage. Not Started = Backlog / Queued. In Progress = Scoping / Design / Development / Evaluation / Delivery. Completed = Done (automatic). Paused or Cancelled freeze the phase where it was. |$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=14))>0 as c3,position($q$| **WBS Status** | Where the plan is: Draft, Awaiting Start, Start Project Declined, Baseline Locked, Changed After Baseline, Ongoing (Training Delivery and Ongoing containers), Closed. |$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=14))>0 as c4,position($q$- **Completed** projects: {success:Completed on time} if$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=14))>0 as c5,position($q$- Progress at 100% but Status not yet Completed: {success:Done on time · close pending} or {gold:Done late · close pending}.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=14))>0 as c6,position($q$| **Start / Due** | Planned dates. Locked once the baseline is approved;$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=14))>0 as c7,position($q$A project is **Completed** when all its work is finished, and **closed** when its WBS has been reviewed and its final numbers locked. Completed comes first; closing is the final sign-off. Click a section below to expand it.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=6))>0 as c8,position($q$| | Project status **Completed** | WBS status **Closed** |
|---|---|---|
| What it means | All work is finished | Final numbers reviewed and locked |
| Who sets it | Project owner (manual) | Close Project request, routed to the first person up the owner's line with the Project Close right (or Full Access) |
| Tasks can be reopened | {success:Yes} — the project moves back to In Progress | {danger:No} — reopen the project through WBS first |
| Follow-up time allowed | {success:Yes} | {danger:No} |
| Existing logs can be corrected | {success:Yes} | {success:Yes} |$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=6))>0 as c9,position($q$### Marking a project Completed
Project status is still set by hand, but Tempo checks the work first:

- A project can be set to **Completed** only when every task is **Done** or **Cancelled**.
- A project with **no tasks** can't be Completed or closed: no tasks means nothing happened. If work was done, add the tasks first; if not, **delete** the project (Tempo offers both options).
- If any task is still open, you'll see the list of open tasks (Task ID, name, status). **Finish** them, or **cancel** the ones that are no longer needed (with a reason) — then set the project to Completed.
- This matches **Actual Progress**: cancelled tasks don't count, so 100% means every remaining task is Done.
- If the whole project was stopped rather than finished, use **Cancelled** or **Paused**, not Completed.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=6))>0 as c10,position($q$### Reopening a task on a Completed project
If a task needs more work after the project was marked Completed, its Immediate Supervisor (or anyone above) can reopen it. Before it happens you'll see a warning, and then:

- the task goes back to **In Progress**, so Actual Progress drops below 100%;
- the project **automatically moves back to In Progress** (the phase moves to the latest In Progress phase);
- the project can only be set to Completed again once that task is Done or Cancelled.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=6))>0 as c11,position($q$When a project is Completed, the owner reviews the WBS and requests closure from the WBS page.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=6))>0 as c12,position($q$**Projects ready to close** lists Completed projects with how long ago they were completed and how many tasks still await validation, with a link to the WBS. **Completed projects have open tasks** flags any Completed project that has open work.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=6))>0 as c13,position($q$- **Projects & Tasks**: the WBS Status column shows a {gold:Ready to close} tag on Completed projects that aren't closed yet.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=6))>0 as c14,position($q$lists projects Completed **14+ days** ago that still aren't closed, so supervisors can follow up.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=6))>0 as c15,position($q$1. Set the project's Status to **Paused** (single project or a bulk selection).$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=8))>0 as c16,position($q$and only an active project (not Draft, Completed, Cancelled or Closed).$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=8))>0 as c17,position($q$1. Set Status back to **In Progress**. This works immediately.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=8))>0 as c18,position($q$A paused project moved straight to Completed or Cancelled doesn't need a schedule review (Completed still requires every task to be Done or Cancelled).$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=8))>0 as c19,position($q$| Sort, group and sub-group, hidden groups, counts | Filters (Status, Owner / Assigned to, My role, Project owner, Attention) |$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=23))>0 as c20,position($q$- **Projects:** Owner, Status, **My role** (Owner / Contributor).$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=23))>0 as c21,position($q$for example *Status: In Progress* from All Active Projects (formerly Active Project Portfolio).$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=23))>0 as c22,position($q$| **Active Projects I Own** | Filters: My role Owner · Status In Progress | Project ID, Project, WBS Status, Status, Health,$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=23))>0 as c23,position($q$| **My Active Projects** | Filters: My role Owner + Contributor · Status In Progress | Project ID, Project, Owner, WBS Status, Health,$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=23))>0 as c24,position($q$| **All My Projects** | Same, any status | As above, plus Status | Same |$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=23))>0 as c25,position($q$The Projects board can be grouped by Phase (default), Status, **Health**, WBS Status,$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=23))>0 as c26,position($q$### Draft plans are private until Start Project$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=22))>0 as c27,position($q$**Request Project Closure** (sends a Close Project request)$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=22))>0 as c28,position($q$| **Everyone else** | See the project row only, marked Draft | As usual |$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=29))>0 as c29,position($q$"Draft" includes projects waiting for Start Project approval.$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=29))>0 as c30,position($q$**Start Project** is the one switch from planning to commitment. Once it's approved:$q$ in (select content from kb_entries where article_number=29))>0 as c31